    {
      "id": "text-126",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1600,
      "width": 1778.7,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 997794,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 13195854,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Reference: briareus-windows. Other clients match this structure, differing only as noted here.\n🎙 Meet is the first header button on a project's page. While a meeting about this project runs it reads '🎙 Meeting ●', and the meeting status leads the subtitle.\nStatus line states: '… · connecting…', then 'm:ss · $x.xxx' followed by listening, speaking, looking it up… or muted, plus ' · <error>' when there is one.\nThe 🎙 Meeting tab (last tab) shows while a meeting runs on the project (with ●) and after it ends. It sticks to the bottom as lines arrive, and before the first line reads 'The assistant is joining. What the meeting says and what\nit answers shows here.'\nErrors and preconditions (missing ElevenLabs voice ID or API key, a meeting already running) are message boxes titled 'Meeting assistant'. Settings live under ⚙ Settings → 🎙 Meeting assistant, which another agent covers.\nThe app list in the join menu comes from the meeting apps that are running (Microsoft Teams, Zoom, Webex, Slack, Discord, browsers as '(Meet)').\nRegion names (sidebar, canvas, raise, sunken) are the theme.* roles; widths and margins are layout.* in tokens/. Greys only, on purpose.",
      "originalText": "Reference: briareus-windows. Other clients match this structure, differing only as noted here.\n🎙 Meet is the first header button on a project's page. While a meeting about this project runs it reads '🎙 Meeting ●', and the meeting status leads the subtitle.\nStatus line states: '… · connecting…', then 'm:ss · $x.xxx' followed by listening, speaking, looking it up… or muted, plus ' · <error>' when there is one.\nThe 🎙 Meeting tab (last tab) shows while a meeting runs on the project (with ●) and after it ends. It sticks to the bottom as lines arrive, and before the first line reads 'The assistant is joining. What the meeting says and what\nit answers shows here.'\nErrors and preconditions (missing ElevenLabs voice ID or API key, a meeting already running) are message boxes titled 'Meeting assistant'. Settings live under ⚙ Settings → 🎙 Meeting assistant, which another agent covers.\nThe app list in the join menu comes from the meeting apps that are running (Microsoft Teams, Zoom, Webex, Slack, Discord, browsers as '(Meet)').\nRegion names (sidebar, canvas, raise, sunken) are the theme.* roles; widths and margins are layout.* in tokens/. Greys only, on purpose.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    }
  ],
